    <briefdescription>
<para>Implementation of <ref refid="structllvm_1_1format__provider" kindref="compound">format_provider&lt;T&gt;</ref> for floating point types. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The options string of a floating point type has the format:</para>
<para>float_options :: [style][precision] style ::  precision :: &lt;non-negative integer&gt; 0-99</para>
<para><hruler/>
 </para>
<sect1 id="structllvm_1_1format__provider_3_01_t_00_01std_1_1enable__if__t_3_01support_1_1detail_1_1use__do0b6e29fefeb3f45b5cb97fc7e03df3df_1autotoc_md52_1s1"><sect2 id="structllvm_1_1format__provider_3_01_t_00_01std_1_1enable__if__t_3_01support_1_1detail_1_1use__do0b6e29fefeb3f45b5cb97fc7e03df3df_1autotoc_md52">
<title>| style | Meaning | Example |</title></sect2></sect1>
<sect1 id="structllvm_1_1format__provider_3_01_t_00_01std_1_1enable__if__t_3_01support_1_1detail_1_1use__do0b6e29fefeb3f45b5cb97fc7e03df3df_1autotoc_md53">
<title>| | | Input | Output |</title><para>| P / p | Percentage | 0.05 | 5.00% | | F / f | Fixed point | 1.0 | 1.00 | | E | Exponential with E | 100000 | 1.0E+05 | | e | Exponential with e | 100000 | 1.0e+05 | </para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="structllvm_1_1format__provider_3_01_t_00_01std_1_1enable__if__t_3_01support_1_1detail_1_1use__do0b6e29fefeb3f45b5cb97fc7e03df3df_1autotoc_md54">
<title>| (empty) | Same as F / f | | |</title><para>The default precision is 6 for exponential (E / e) and 2 for everything else. </para>
</sect1>
